{
  "id": "T18_65_a_story_with_no_period_through_a_normalization_reads_not_started_before_its_since",
  "family": "T18",
  "rules": [
    "7.6.12",
    "7.6.5",
    "7.6.6",
    "7.6.14",
    "7.2.6",
    "7.2.7",
    "9.5.2",
    "9.5.3",
    "9.5.8",
    "4.2.5",
    "12.19",
    "12.20"
  ],
  "description": "The project is normalized under the fixture fire-rating interpretation from Wednesday. On Thursday A-601 shows Door 103 as \"90 min\" at 09:00 and the specification \"1.5 h\" at 11:00, and A-601 revises Door 104 from Monday's \"1.5 h\" to \"90 min\". The stories an application records anyway have no period. Each end act has cause normalization, cites the normalization, has no time, and carries since: the instant the sides first differ literally (Thursday 11:00), or the revision's occurrence time (Thursday 09:00). Each story reads not_started, with no ending, at cutoffs before its since, and ended from it. Door 113's sides are dated by day, so its since is Thursday: a Thursday-noon cutoff is neither before it nor at or after it, and the open dimension reads ambiguous. No listing read lists these stories. Door 123's story is like Door 103's until a correction shows that the specification said \"90 min\": its sides never differed even literally, so the correction revises the end act to cause correction, without since, and the story reads ended at every cutoff, Wednesday included.",
  "note": "7.6.12: \"for a normalization, cause `normalization`, with as its record the normalization or normalizations that put the story's interpretation in force: for a conflict story, at the instant at which its interval would begin under literal comparison (7.2.6) ... for a change story, at its revised Assertion's occurrence time (7.2.7). The end act also carries `since`: that instant\"; \"Reads report the story as ended at every cutoff with an empty interval (9.5.2), except that a story whose ending is a normalization reads `not_started` at a cutoff before its `since`, and ended at a cutoff that its `since` is at or before (4.2.5). Where neither holds, its open dimension is ambiguous (4.5.3).\" 7.6.12, order of precedence: \"`correction` applies when, without the corrections, the story would have a period under its interpretation, or would have one under literal comparison while in the corrected account it has none under literal comparison.\" 4.2.5: \"A is *at or before* B when A's interval ends no later than B's interval ends\", so Thursday 11:00 is at or before a Thursday-noon cutoff and a Thursday date is not.",
